<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Analysis>
    <Title>Credentials - Cached Login Creds - Windows</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<P>This analysis grabs information on the current cached logon credentials on a Windows system.</P>
<P>This analysis scraps information put in place by <STRONG>Fixlet: Invoke - Windows Cached Credentials Probe - Windows</STRONG></P>
<P>Information provided by this fixlet is useful in determining which user accounts need password resets if a machine is compromised.</P>
<P>Information on using this content is available here: <A href="https://github.com/strawgate/C3-Protect/wiki/Windows-Credentials">https://github.com/strawgate/C3-Protect/wiki/Windows-Credentials</A></P>
<P>For general information or to report issues with C3 Protect content please visit GitHub here: <A href="https://github.com/strawgate/C3-Protect">https://github.com/strawgate/C3-Protect</A></P>]]></Description>
    <Relevance>windows of operating system</Relevance>
    <Relevance>exists file &quot;CachedUsers.txt&quot; of folder &quot;WinCreds&quot; of folder &quot;__Global&quot; of data folder of client</Relevance>
    <Domain>BESC</Domain>
    <Property ID="1" Name="Credentials - Cached Logon Credentials - Windows" EvaluationPeriod="P1D">(concatenations &quot;&quot; of substrings separated by &quot;%00&quot; of (following text of first &quot;%ff%fe&quot; of it | it)) of lines whose (it !=&quot;%00&quot;) of file &quot;CachedUsers.txt&quot; of folder &quot;WinCreds&quot; of folder &quot;__Global&quot; of folder &quot;C:\Program Files (x86)\BigFix Enterprise\BES Client\__BESData\&quot;</Property>
  </Analysis>
</BES>
